{"tool": "worker-06/check_class_binding.py", "rules_version": "w06-draft-3", "gate_id": "G-CLASSBIND", "generated_at": "2026-09-12T00:36:39+08:00", "source": "schemas/af_wcc_vacuum.yaml", "doc_sha256": "cce9c60146d6a907082ade91c67c8ac658bd796d1241f9bb8965c3d2aa69daa3", "rules_sha256": "a30606136747fc76ac4defd0efb9c985aae1efd60f9d0d916910f2ae292298a7", "verdict": "fail", "checks": [{"check_id": "single_class_id", "verdict": "pass", "detail": "class id 'AF-WCC-VAC-GEN' (family WCC)", "evidence": {"class_id": "AF-WCC-VAC-GEN"}}, {"check_id": "declared_artifact_matches", "verdict": "pass", "detail": "node/artifact fields agree with map declaration", "evidence": {"map_node": "F1", "allowed_artifacts": ["schemas/af_wcc_vacuum.yaml"]}}, {"check_id": "no_composite_regularity_string", "verdict": "fail", "detail": "composite regularity strings: ['c0 or c2', 'c2 or c0', 'c2/c0']", "evidence": {"matches": ["c0 or c2", "c2 or c0", "c2/c0"]}}, {"check_id": "regularity_selector", "verdict": "fail", "detail": "WCC class carries an SCC-style regularity selector ['2'] (class leakage)", "evidence": {}}, {"check_id": "required_slots", "verdict": "pass", "detail": "all required slots present", "evidence": {"missing": [], "present_by_key": ["quantifiers", "topology", "data_class", "genericity", "future_null_infinity", "visibility", "conclusion_type"], "present_by_text_only": []}}, {"check_id": "quantifier_completeness", "verdict": "pass", "detail": "universal + existential quantifiers present", "evidence": {}}, {"check_id": "genericity_qualified", "verdict": "pass", "detail": "genericity carries a qualifier: ['gen', 'residual_comeager', 'the constraint manifold x^r_vac(af) of one-ended asymptotically flat vacuum initial data in the declared regularity class, carrying the topology induced from the weighted sobolev product h^s_delta x h^{s-1}_{delta+1}. r1 f04 accepted: the topology is the subspace topology on the constraint set, not the topology of the unconstrained product (under the latter reading x_vac itself is meager and no g exists). x_vac is a closed subset of a banach space, hence a baire space, so comeagerness is non-vacuous and g is non-empty.', 'subspace topology induced on x^r_vac(af); frechet topology for the smooth-with-decay class. gauge invariance is handled by noting every predicate here is diffeomorphism invariant; the quotient by asymptotically-identity diffeomorphisms is not used to define comeagerness and remains an open technical gap (see unresolved_items).', 'g = intersection over n >= 1 of u_n with each u_n open and dense in x^r_vac(af); equivalently the complement is meager (first category); g_r is non-empty because x_vac is baire', 'the excluded set is required to be meager; whether the named candidate families are meager is unresolved, so they are listed as obligations rather than as constructions. candidates: data with a nonzero killing field, data in the exactly-extendible (cauchy-horizon) family, self-similar or scale-invariant data, finite-dimensional analytic families generated by continuation, and exactly symmetric data (see axis_registry and membership_ruling).', 'unresolved', 'true', 'set-level only: the class quantifies over a comeager set g of data; the schema does not decide membership of an individual datum. a single symmetric/stationary datum is expected outside g in the vacuum class, but that expectation is a proof obligation, not a schema field (flash-04 amb-07 ruling).', 'artifacts/formulation/vocab_aliases.json', 'true', \"genericity is part of the class identity. the comeager form is this class. 'for all data' is strictly stronger. the dense-open form is also strictly stronger, because a dense open set is comeager (it is the countable intersection of the constant family). the comeager form does not imply the dense-open form (a comeager set can have empty interior). no strengthening may be substituted silently. see genericity.transfer_failures for the two directions.\", \"astra f1 acceptance names 'open dense'. this schema's frozen default is the residual/comeager form; open_dense_escape is registered below as a distinct strictly stronger variant (a dense open set is comeager, so it implies the default) and is never silently substituted. a gate matching only the literal words 'open dense' would accept a stronger class than this one - recorded as a vocabulary risk.\", 'residual_comeager', 'full_measure', 'no_transfer', 'let c = intersection over n of u_n with each u_n open dense and of measure < 1/n; c is comeager and lebesgue-null, so comeagerness does not yield full measure (a single fat-cantor complement is open dense but not null, which is why the countable intersection is used) [r1 f03]', 'standard_fact', 'unresolved', 'full_measure', 'residual_comeager', 'no_transfer', 'let c be the comeager null set of the row above; then x minus c is meager and has full measure, so full measure does not yield comeagerness. (the irrationals are both comeager and full-measure and therefore witness nothing - r1 f03.)', 'standard_fact', 'unresolved', 'residual_comeager', 'open_dense_escape', 'no_transfer', 'the irrationals are comeager with empty interior: a comeager set need not contain any nonempty open subset, so the comeager form does not yield a dense-open form', 'standard_fact', 'unresolved', 'residual_comeager', 'finite_codimension_complement', 'no_transfer', 'a fat cantor set is nowhere dense (meager) yet has positive measure, so it is not contained in any countable union of finite-codimension submanifolds, which is null', 'elementary', 'n/a', 'open_dense_escape', 'residual_comeager', 'transfers', 'a dense open set u is the countable intersection of the constant family {u}, hence comeager; the dense-open form implies the comeager form', 'elementary', 'n/a', 'finite_codimension_complement', 'residual_comeager', 'transfers', 'a proper closed finite-codimension submanifold is closed and nowhere dense, so a countable union of them is meager; if the exceptional set is so covered, the property holds on a comeager set', 'elementary', 'n/a', 'open_dense_escape', 'strictly_stronger', 'false', 'implies residual_comeager', 'dense_escape', 'strictly_weaker', 'false', 'implied by residual_comeager in a baire space (a comeager set is dense); a dense set need not be comeager, so it is strictly weaker than the class default. [r2-16 corrected: was off-vocabulary and mislabelled incomparable]', 'full_measure', 'incomparable', 'false', 'a specified measure on x, e.g. a gaussian measure induced by the constraint map', 'none', 'strictly_stronger', 'false', \"tier 1 refutes the class by showing the not-p set is non-meager in the ambient space (equivalently: it meets every comeager set). exhibiting a single datum with not-p is not sufficient in general: g is existentially quantified and the schema's membership_ruling leaves individual membership undecided, so the datum may lie outside every admissible witness g. if the class is instantiated with a concrete, explicitly constructed generic set g*, then one datum in g* with not-p refutes the instantiated statement - a different, hypothesis-stronger claim. route r1 = non-meagerness (general refutation); route r2 = a datum in an instantiated g* (instantiated claims only). [r1 f01 accepted; the earlier text wrongly made r1 a general route]\"]", "evidence": {}}, {"check_id": "conclusion_family_match", "verdict": "fail", "detail": "conclusion ['true', 'true', \"there is no visible_singularity_from_i_plus: for every future-inextendible causal geodesic gamma of finite affine length, for every q in i+ and every t0 in [0,t), the tail gamma([t0,t)) is not contained in j^-(q) intersect m - no single point of i+ causally precedes the singular end of gamma. this is not equivalent to 'gamma is contained in b = m minus j^-(i+)': b-containment is strictly stronger, and a geodesic may begin in j^-(i+) and end in the black-hole region. [r1 f02 accepted; the earlier 'i.e. inside b' equivalence was false]\", 'weak_cosmic_censorship', 'open_problem', 'wcc', 'generic asymptotically flat vacuum initial data have a maximal development with complete future null infinity and no singularity visible from future null infinity.', 'forall r in d0 exists g_r comeager forall d in g_r: af_{i+}(m_d) and complete(i+_d) and not exists visible_singularity_from_i_plus(m_d)', 'non_vacuity is a well-formedness condition on the class (it must admit data with a future-incomplete development), not a conjunct of the mathematical statement above. [r1 minor]', 'future asymptotic predictability: there exists a partial cauchy surface s, asymptotically flat, whose future domain of dependence has i+ in its closure', 'claimed equivalence, unverified; the class is bound to statement_formal, and a citation of the equivalent phrasing must carry l1 verification', 'black-hole region non-empty (black-hole formation is a separate statement and is not part of this conclusion)', 'geodesic completeness of m', 'c2 or c0 inextendibility of the maximal development (scc content)', 'absence of singularities anywhere', 'the statement for all data rather than for generic data', 'dropping i+ completeness', \"replacing the generic quantifier with 'there exist data'\", \"replacing 'no visible singularity' by 'no singularity'\", 'using a weaker visibility notion or a different definition of singular point', 'epistemic_status=open_problem; recording conclusion_type=theorem requires artifact_refs with a checked proof and is auto-rejected otherwise'] uses tokens from the other family: ['inextendib']", "evidence": {}}, {"check_id": "theorem_requires_artifact_refs", "verdict": "pass", "detail": "not a theorem conclusion; guard not triggered", "evidence": {}}, {"check_id": "no_conclusion_inflation", "verdict": "pass", "detail": "no prove/establish-theorem phrase", "evidence": {"matches": []}}, {"check_id": "no_cross_domain_contamination", "verdict": "pass", "detail": "no base-repo contamination tokens", "evidence": {"matches": []}}]}
